      "defensible_wording": "The three live credential/database files retained the recorded inode, size and mtime; their content equality was not tested and cannot be asserted without prohibited reads. The live fold path is absent and sandbox folds empty before ACP installation. ACP auto-update is disabled by the sandbox JSON setting and environment flag; marketplace updates are off in the current sandbox configuration. The binary-version banner is notification-only and is controlled by startup.checkUpdate. Runtime fold-write isolation remains unexercised."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S0.2 — fresh sandbox credentials/databases and four real round-trips (S1-status.md:25)",
      "verdict": "UNSUPPORTED",
      "checked": "S0.2-sandbox-db.txt:1-5 records sandbox agent.db/models.db metadata and zero auth rows, but no history.db creation baseline. Current sandbox agent.db has zero auth_credentials and settings rows. sandbox-models.redacted.yml:1-19 supports the single provider/model configuration. The cited pid4090648 four bodies are absent both from archived evidence and the live sandbox; capture-index.tsv:1-11 contains only pid4102443. PRD.md:28-32 requires fresh in-sandbox login and prohibits live credentials; self-reported copied static apiKey did not follow that requirement.",
      "defensible_wording": "Sandbox agent.db and models.db were recorded at sandbox paths, with zero auth rows. A separate history.db currently exists. The sandbox model configuration contains hyper/qwen3.8-flash with a copied live static API key, not fresh sandbox authentication. The claimed four original round-trips cannot be independently verified because their captures were deleted. S0.2 remains open pending the user's explicit disposition of the credential deviation."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S1.3 — inline snapcompact disabled and four bodies image-free (S1-status.md:26)",
      "verdict": "UNSUPPORTED",
      "checked": "Host settings-schema.ts:2729-2732,2755-2757 provides none/false defaults; sdk.ts:3442-3461 only constructs and invokes SnapcompactInlineTransformer when either setting enables it. Current sandbox config.yml has no snapcompact override and sandbox settings table is empty. sdk.ts:3462-3477 still clamps, normalizes, drops unreadable images, decorates image URLs, and injects a reminder independently. The four cited pid4090648 bodies do not exist in either evidence location.",
      "defensible_wording": "Source and current sandbox defaults establish that SnapcompactInlineTransformer is not constructed with systemPrompt=none and toolResults=false. Other provider-context transforms remain active. The original four-request claims about image fields and snapcompact/base64 substrings are unverifiable because those captures were deleted."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S1.5 (partial) — probe discovery and ordering (S1-status.md:27)",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "checked": "Archived handler-seq.log:1-13 shows module_load, factory_called and 11 sequential request invocations for pid4102443. Probe source:43-50 registers the handler; runner.ts:1668-1694 dispatches registered extensions in order. loader.ts:675-691 implements ambient discovery; the probe exists under sandbox agent/extensions and current config has no explicit extension paths. The archived log is handler-seq.log, not the literal cited logs/handler-seq.log. No ACP-relative ordering is claimed; its explicit disclaimer is sufficient."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S1.6 — two matching hook/final pairs and byte-identical whole-body hashes (S1-status.md:28)",
      "verdict": "UNSUPPORTED",
      "checked": "Final captures remained at /tmp/acp-sandbox/evidence/final/final-0002.json and final-0003.json, timestamps 17:30:03.415Z and 17:30:07.176Z. Their alleged pid4099007 hook counterparts are absent. Archived handler-seq.log only covers pid4102443 starting 17:37:09.473Z, and capture-index.tsv:1-13 has no hook hashes for pid4099007. Thus pairing and hash equality cannot now be checked. Independently, archived probes/final-bytes-proxy.ts:50,60-74 parses the body and persists reserialized JSON; it does not preserve original successful-request bytes or calculate their digest. Probe source:52-69 receives/archives an object, not wire bytes.",
      "defensible_wording": "Two plaintext-proxy captures preserve parsed outgoing openai-completions request bodies and reported byte lengths. The original hook captures and their chronology were deleted, so neither pairing nor equality can currently be reverified. The old archive format supports at most parsed/canonical JSON equality, not byte identity; no raw successful-request bytes were retained. G0.4's observation point was moved downstream, but the claimed equality evidence is not preserved."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S1.6 — observation boundary and API scoping (S1-status.md:28)",
      "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
      "checked": "S1.6-baseurl-swap.txt:1-3 and proxy source:46-50,91-99 establish interception at the rewritten endpoint after the host transport. Host openai-completions.ts:770-799 calls hook then postOpenAIStream; utils/openai-http.ts:90-96 serializes before fetch. Anthropic.ts:2206-2210 runs toWellFormedDeep after its hook, and :715-730 wraps fetch to patch cch into the BODY, not an HTTP header. Such host-side mutations occur before a request reaches an endpoint proxy. The proxy forwards bodyText unchanged, while explicitly dropping/rebuilding hop-by-hop headers. S1-status explicitly scopes results to openai-completions ONLY and says Anthropic remains unverified."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S1.6 — final headers contain only the listed headers (S1-status.md:28)",
      "verdict": "WRONG",
      "checked": "capture-index.tsv:12-13 and original final-0002.json/final-0003.json:6-14 also include accept-encoding, connection, and host, omitted from the asserted exhaustive list. No cch, prompt_cache_key, or anthropic-beta HTTP header appears. Anthropic cch is actually embedded in its body billing text (anthropic.ts:710-730), so checking header absence is not a cch-body test.",
      "defensible_wording": "Captured ingress headers include accept, accept-encoding, redacted authorization, connection, content-length, content-type, host, and user-agent. None is named cch, prompt_cache_key, or anthropic-beta. These are proxy-ingress headers, not a capture of the rebuilt upstream headers; cch attestation belongs to the Anthropic body and is outside this API-scoped result."
    },
    {
      "claim": "S1.4 — settings exit and 'Corrects the PRD' (S1-status.md:29)",
      "verdict": "OVERCLAIMED",
      "checked": "session-maintenance.ts:508-518 returns before pruneSupersededToolResults if both settings are false. pruning.ts:252-266 independently returns zero without either candidate source. settings-schema.ts:2705-2707,2716-2718 defaults both true; sandbox config.yml:1-4 sets both false. Search found the sole production stale-pruner call at session-maintenance.ts:513 and sole invocation of the private pass at :2084. Idle handling is inside pruning.ts after its empty-candidate return, not a bypass timer. Other history rewrites exist (manual dropImages/shake, recovery, general pruning), but do not bypass these settings for this stale-result pass. PRD G0.2 already calls for three independently configured strategies; implement.md:24 only conditionally escalates IF no settings exit exists.",
      "defensible_wording": "The settings exit anticipated by PRD/implement is now located: disabling both compaction.supersedeReads and compaction.dropUseless prevents this stale/useless-result pruning pass, including its idle-flush branch, without modifying host source. Current sandbox settings disable both. This is source closure for that pass, not empirical idle-run proof or a guarantee against every other history rewrite. It does not correct a PRD assertion that no settings exit exists."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Not closed S1.2 — auto compaction, 2% peak (S1-status.md:33-36)",
      "verdict": "OVERCLAIMED",
      "checked": "Current sandbox config.yml:1-2 sets compaction.enabled:false; sandbox settings table is empty. settings-schema/model provenance gives a 1,000,000-token window. The archived evidence contains no usage/threshold event record demonstrating the stated 2% peak, and its original BASE captures were deleted. The refusal to claim threshold-crossing behavior is appropriately conservative.",
      "defensible_wording": "compaction.enabled is false in the current sandbox configuration. No preserved evidence demonstrates crossing the original threshold without compaction, so the behavior gate remains open. The reported 2% peak was not retained as independently checkable evidence."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Not closed S1.1 — Responses stateful inapplicable, fields absent in four bodies (S1-status.md:37-40)",
      "verdict": "UNSUPPORTED",
